<title>FRANCE: Paris air cargo import traffic up 4.2 pct in Q1.</title>
<headline>Paris air cargo import traffic up 4.2 pct in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-March 1997 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 134,296 tonnes, up 4.2 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The Paris airports' January-March 1997 import traffic, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on January-March 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>Domestic	   6,920	  down 11.4 percent</p>
<p>European Union  16,350	   up  16.4</p>
<p>Non-EU Europe    3,124	   up  14.5</p>
<p>North Africa     2,958	  down 25.9</p>
<p>Sub-Saharan Africa</p>
<p>		    14,628	  down  1 4</p>
<p>North America   43,417	  down  4.3</p>
<p>French territories</p>
<p>		     3,718	    up 11.0</p>
<p>Latin America    5,421	    up  8.0</p>
<p>Middle East	6,190	    up  1.9</p>
<p>Far East	  31,570	    up 22.9</p>
<p>  Total	  134,296	    up  4.2</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
</text>
